    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "After the mid-season firing, the franchise brought in John Tortorella, a stabilizing leader who provided steadying leadership. His coaching performance, a winning record, and successful interim management guided the team through hardship, leading to playoff series victories. However, this defensive dominance over a weakened attack was the final blow for the vulnerable athletes on the opposing side.",
